1
00:00:00,570 --> 00:00:03,470
Okay, put it here. Perfect.

2
00:00:04,710 --> 00:00:07,356
You know, this should be really delicious.

3
00:00:08,018 --> 00:00:09,785
I know, I know. I focused on this adobo.

4
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,373
Don’t worry, it’s good.

5
00:00:11,499 --> 00:00:15,024
Because, you know, Mom and
Dad need to be happy since we

6
00:00:15,048 --> 00:00:19,024
have to tell them the truth—we
need to go back to Singapore.

7
00:00:21,114 --> 00:00:23,300
Yeah. Also, Anne and I are together now.

8
00:00:23,498 --> 00:00:25,258
Hey! Why not one at a time?

9
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,406
Like, one thing at a time?

10
00:00:26,431 --> 00:00:29,094
No, Tash. We should
say everything all at once.

11
00:00:29,898 --> 00:00:30,907
Hey.

12
00:00:31,152 --> 00:00:31,505
Right?

13
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:34,868
Your adobo better be
really good, my goodness.

14
00:00:35,245 --> 00:00:36,725
Mom, Dad?

15
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,438
Food is ready!

16
00:00:38,515 --> 00:00:40,355
Lola Maxi, let’s eat!

17
00:00:40,424 --> 00:00:42,024
Okay, here we come!

18
00:00:42,441 --> 00:00:43,621
Hey, food’s ready!

19
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:47,673
Oh wow! Smells amazing!

20
00:00:47,705 --> 00:00:49,410
You made this?!

21
00:00:49,435 --> 00:00:50,495
Yes.

22
00:00:52,047 --> 00:00:53,760
- The smell is incredible!
- So fragrant!

23
00:00:53,785 --> 00:00:55,742
Tell them what’s on the menu.

24
00:00:55,767 --> 00:00:57,932
- So, we have adobo…
- This is so good!

25
00:00:57,957 --> 00:00:59,083
- Adobo?!
- Yeah!

26
00:00:59,212 --> 00:01:00,272
Okoy!

27
00:01:00,843 --> 00:01:01,749
You made this?!

28
00:01:01,774 --> 00:01:06,121
Dad, this is the Andres special
signature adobo dish of the nation.

29
00:01:06,152 --> 00:01:08,211
Without the orange octopus.

30
00:01:08,243 --> 00:01:09,603
Let’s taste it!

31
00:01:09,628 --> 00:01:10,760
- Go ahead!
- You, my love?

32
00:01:10,785 --> 00:01:12,428
It smells different… you can already tell!

33
00:01:13,148 --> 00:01:14,328
Thank you, thank you!

34
00:01:14,889 --> 00:01:19,063
Delicious! Wow, this is
amazing. It tastes special.

35
00:01:19,088 --> 00:01:20,408
- But wait…
- Yes?

36
00:01:20,924 --> 00:01:24,650
You know, when things like this
happen, there are only two reasons.

37
00:01:24,675 --> 00:01:25,624
It does taste different!

38
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,313
Either you’re confessing to something,
or you’re making an announcement.

39
00:01:33,353 --> 00:01:35,368
Oh no, Lola, there’s
nothing! Nothing at all.

40
00:01:35,393 --> 00:01:36,745
It’s just…

41
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:38,411
Just try it, go on. Try it.

42
00:01:38,995 --> 00:01:40,589
- Are you happy?
- What you said is true.

43
00:01:40,833 --> 00:01:41,826
- Huh?
- It’s delicious.

44
00:01:41,853 --> 00:01:42,699
What announcement?

45
00:01:42,841 --> 00:01:44,261
Ah, okay, I’ll just say it.

46
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:48,820
Uh, Mom, Dad, Lola Maxi… um…

47
00:01:49,395 --> 00:01:51,001
Tash! Let me do it!

48
00:01:52,871 --> 00:01:56,264
Mom, Dad, I have something to confess.

49
00:01:57,130 --> 00:01:57,650
What?

50
00:01:59,914 --> 00:02:00,421
Hey!

51
00:02:00,446 --> 00:02:01,974
- Hey! Water!
- Oh no!

52
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:03,690
Oh no!

53
00:02:04,053 --> 00:02:05,446
I’m getting nervous.

54
00:02:05,471 --> 00:02:06,636
- Why?
- Why?

55
00:02:06,661 --> 00:02:07,854
What are you two about to say?

56
00:02:10,858 --> 00:02:12,212
Well, Tash, what do you want to say?

57
00:02:12,681 --> 00:02:20,052
Wow, the food is really delicious! I
should taste how good it is, right?!

58
00:03:23,843 --> 00:03:24,953
This is your fault!

59
00:03:26,744 --> 00:03:27,734
You know why?!

60
00:03:27,897 --> 00:03:28,566
Why?

61
00:03:28,591 --> 00:03:32,891
You made the food too good,
that’s why we couldn’t confess!

62
00:03:34,051 --> 00:03:35,133
What?!

63
00:03:35,403 --> 00:03:37,923
If it’s good, it’s wrong. If
it’s bad, it’s also wrong.

64
00:03:39,194 --> 00:03:40,312
Where do I even stand?!

65
00:03:41,686 --> 00:03:43,646
Fine, let’s just do this.

66
00:03:44,362 --> 00:03:48,889
At the right time, we’ll tell Mom and
Dad we’re going back to Singapore, okay?

67
00:03:50,004 --> 00:03:50,883
Okay.

68
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:52,970
What?! Huh?!

69
00:03:53,773 --> 00:03:54,840
Wait, wait, wait!

70
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:56,734
You’re leaving?!

71
00:03:57,288 --> 00:03:58,781
Did I hear that right?!

72
00:03:59,385 --> 00:04:00,898
Kuya Chard, what are you doing here?

73
00:04:01,025 --> 00:04:04,697
Looking for a signal, but then
my SIM card fell on the floor.

74
00:04:05,014 --> 00:04:07,341
Wait, you’re leaving?!

75
00:04:07,366 --> 00:04:08,980
- Sssh!
- Keep quiet!

76
00:04:09,005 --> 00:04:10,538
- Don’t say anything, don’t say anything!
- Quiet!

77
00:04:10,563 --> 00:04:13,487
Mom and Dad don’t know
yet. Don’t say anything, okay?

78
00:04:13,547 --> 00:04:16,742
Or else, the whole
Barangay Singko will find out.

79
00:04:17,425 --> 00:04:21,339
What do I do? I can’t keep secrets!

80
00:04:21,364 --> 00:04:23,685
Especially about Andres
and Anne’s situation.

81
00:04:23,825 --> 00:04:24,764
What?

82
00:04:24,789 --> 00:04:25,750
You don’t know?

83
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:26,853
You two are together?!

84
00:04:26,878 --> 00:04:29,434
Sssh! Don’t say it! Someone might hear you!

85
00:04:29,827 --> 00:04:30,720
What?!

86
00:04:31,527 --> 00:04:32,578
Andres!

87
00:04:35,643 --> 00:04:37,363
Kuya Iske, what are you doing here?

88
00:04:37,446 --> 00:04:39,599
Fixing the firewood for our chimney.

89
00:04:40,387 --> 00:04:41,773
Did I hear that right?!

90
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:43,378
That?

91
00:04:43,403 --> 00:04:45,091
- You and Anne are together?!
- Sssh!

92
00:04:45,474 --> 00:04:47,507
Don’t say it! Kuya Iske, stay quiet.

93
00:04:47,532 --> 00:04:49,841
Is it true—oh… sorry, sorry! Is it true?!

94
00:04:49,866 --> 00:04:51,059
- When are you going to tell—
- Ssshh!

95
00:04:51,072 --> 00:04:52,399
Hey, what’s going on?

96
00:04:52,424 --> 00:04:53,630
Andres and Anne are together!

97
00:04:54,174 --> 00:04:55,184
Yeah!

98
00:04:55,373 --> 00:04:56,433
You said it?!

99
00:04:56,464 --> 00:04:57,192
They already knew.

100
00:04:57,217 --> 00:04:58,193
- Of course!
- How did you know?

101
00:04:58,218 --> 00:05:01,492
It was obvious! Right, Grandma?

102
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,560
Right? I told you, Orb!

103
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:04,825
Yeah.

104
00:05:05,283 --> 00:05:06,180
Well…

105
00:05:06,205 --> 00:05:08,865
Ssh, don’t say it! Lola Maxi,
don’t say anything, okay?

106
00:05:09,191 --> 00:05:10,111
Clap—

107
00:05:10,136 --> 00:05:11,604
Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry!

108
00:05:13,117 --> 00:05:16,467
Hey, my boyfriend is so serious!

109
00:05:16,648 --> 00:05:20,015
Boyfriend! It still feels
weird calling you that.

110
00:05:20,772 --> 00:05:22,792
I haven’t even told Tso K yet.

111
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,253
Maybe tell him when he’s in a good mood?

112
00:05:25,884 --> 00:05:26,958
Mmm.

113
00:05:26,985 --> 00:05:30,438
But you know, there’s something important
I need to tell my special girlfriend.

114
00:05:31,891 --> 00:05:32,891
What is it?

115
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:38,234
Anne, my job in Singapore
has been calling me.

116
00:05:39,065 --> 00:05:40,005
Hmmm?

117
00:05:44,237 --> 00:05:45,231
Hey!

118
00:05:46,258 --> 00:05:47,255
Why so close?

119
00:05:48,017 --> 00:05:49,083
Twelve inches apart!

120
00:05:50,148 --> 00:05:51,601
Leave some space!

121
00:05:52,789 --> 00:05:54,089
There, that’s better!

122
00:05:56,678 --> 00:05:59,065
Tso K, who’s that with you?

123
00:05:59,518 --> 00:06:00,931
This is Charity.

124
00:06:02,022 --> 00:06:03,835
She’s our new masseuse.

125
00:06:04,294 --> 00:06:08,617
Oh, to help with our
growing business, SpaKarl.

126
00:06:08,642 --> 00:06:09,691
Wow!

127
00:06:10,275 --> 00:06:12,221
- Hello, nice to meet you!
- Hi…

128
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:13,643
Hi, Charity!

129
00:06:13,668 --> 00:06:17,242
Charity, all set? You
can start working now.

130
00:06:17,415 --> 00:06:18,513
Thank you!

131
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:20,597
See?

132
00:06:20,655 --> 00:06:25,552
You can tell our business is growing
because we’re hiring more employees!

133
00:06:25,577 --> 00:06:27,887
- Yeah, Tso K!
- Oh, see, Charity is an addition!

134
00:06:28,038 --> 00:06:29,458
That means success!

135
00:06:29,495 --> 00:06:31,702
SpaKarl is successful!

136
00:06:31,877 --> 00:06:34,337
So that means you’re in a good mood today?

137
00:06:34,376 --> 00:06:37,183
Of course! Is there any
reason to be in a bad mood?

138
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,887
We’re happy today!

139
00:06:38,939 --> 00:06:42,226
If that’s the case, I have
something to tell you.

140
00:06:42,308 --> 00:06:44,753
Oh? Okay, go ahead.

141
00:06:44,846 --> 00:06:47,406
You? You’re my favorite niece!

142
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:49,353
Go, go, go!

143
00:06:49,791 --> 00:06:53,065
Tso K, what if… I get a boyfriend?

144
00:06:56,556 --> 00:06:57,704
Boyfriend?

145
00:06:58,485 --> 00:07:00,005
Oh, boyfriend!

146
00:07:03,575 --> 00:07:04,698
Wait a second.

147
00:07:04,723 --> 00:07:06,181
- Why?
- Wait.

148
00:07:06,265 --> 00:07:08,625
Wow, Tso K seems so cool with it.

149
00:07:10,490 --> 00:07:11,357
Where is he?!

150
00:07:11,803 --> 00:07:12,796
Call him!

151
00:07:12,821 --> 00:07:14,154
That so-called boyfriend!

152
00:07:14,307 --> 00:07:16,373
Bring him here, let me cripple him!

153
00:07:16,398 --> 00:07:17,360
Ah…

154
00:07:17,385 --> 00:07:20,782
Why are you even thinking about
that?! What are you planning?!

155
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:22,280
Oh, you get a boyfriend?

156
00:07:22,453 --> 00:07:23,766
Then what, you’ll
run away together?!

157
00:07:23,835 --> 00:07:24,734
What happens next?

158
00:07:24,759 --> 00:07:25,666
Oh, you get pregnant?!

159
00:07:25,691 --> 00:07:27,461
Then you’ll get married?!

160
00:07:27,486 --> 00:07:29,236
And then what? You’ll have a child?!

161
00:07:29,262 --> 00:07:31,402
Oh, and then what? You expect
me to take care of your child?!

162
00:07:31,806 --> 00:07:34,026
Bring him to me! Where is he, call him now!

163
00:07:34,051 --> 00:07:35,525
- Ah…
- I should go now, I need to go home.

164
00:07:35,550 --> 00:07:36,732
Tso K, I need to go home.

165
00:07:36,757 --> 00:07:38,416
- No, no, no. Don’t leave.
- I should go, I should go.

166
00:07:38,441 --> 00:07:40,035
- No, no, no. Help me find—
- They need me. They need me, Tso K.

167
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:41,095
Help me!

168
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:42,297
Okay, bye-bye, thank you!

169
00:07:42,676 --> 00:07:43,663
Why did he leave?!

170
00:07:43,688 --> 00:07:48,963
Tso K! I said, what IF!
What IF! There’s nothing—

171
00:07:48,988 --> 00:07:51,783
- Just if?
- Just if! Just if.

172
00:07:52,125 --> 00:07:53,259
Oh okay, then!

173
00:07:53,968 --> 00:07:55,853
Andres didn’t even help you?

174
00:08:01,877 --> 00:08:04,250
Atasha, I have to go.

175
00:08:04,276 --> 00:08:07,263
I’m visiting a friend, I might be out late.

176
00:08:07,288 --> 00:08:11,030
Me too, I have to buy some
ingredients, I might take a while.

177
00:08:11,210 --> 00:08:12,157
- Is that okay?
- Go ahead, go ahead.

178
00:08:12,182 --> 00:08:13,616
- Okay!
- Take care on the road, okay?

179
00:08:13,641 --> 00:08:14,547
- Alright, okay!
- Take care!

180
00:08:14,572 --> 00:08:15,911
- Okay, see you!
- Okay.

181
00:08:16,402 --> 00:08:17,308
Bye-bye!

182
00:08:23,058 --> 00:08:23,871
Tash!

183
00:08:25,028 --> 00:08:26,275
Oh, where were you?

184
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,113
Just with Anne.

185
00:08:27,716 --> 00:08:29,863
You know, we almost got caught by Tso K!

186
00:08:30,167 --> 00:08:31,193
So scary!

187
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:35,629
But did you tell the truth about you two?

188
00:08:35,923 --> 00:08:36,576
Not yet.

189
00:08:36,630 --> 00:08:43,903
I’m still looking for the right
timing, but it hasn’t come yet.

190
00:08:43,928 --> 00:08:45,805
And… I don’t have money for a date.

191
00:08:46,078 --> 00:08:51,056
How about this—have a date here at
home, since Mom and Dad aren’t here, right?

192
00:08:51,267 --> 00:08:54,444
You could have a
candlelit dinner, you know!

193
00:08:54,850 --> 00:08:58,030
Actually, that could
work for our first date.

194
00:08:58,703 --> 00:09:00,240
- Yeah!
- It’s a good idea!

195
00:09:00,264 --> 00:09:01,164
Right, and then—

196
00:09:01,190 --> 00:09:01,891
What?!

197
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:05,830
You and Anne are having a date at home?!

198
00:09:05,855 --> 00:09:06,643
- Huh?
- No!

199
00:09:06,668 --> 00:09:08,738
Nosy frog, huh?!

200
00:09:08,983 --> 00:09:10,843
Nosy frog? I heard that!

201
00:09:10,912 --> 00:09:12,972
We were cleaning, we heard it!

202
00:09:13,121 --> 00:09:13,708
Yeah!

203
00:09:13,733 --> 00:09:15,349
And we can’t keep it a secret!

204
00:09:15,374 --> 00:09:16,742
Andres!

205
00:09:17,235 --> 00:09:18,302
Andres!

206
00:09:18,636 --> 00:09:21,790
Andres, congratulations! I knew it!

207
00:09:21,815 --> 00:09:24,389
You and Anne were endgame!

208
00:09:24,414 --> 00:09:25,960
Yes!

209
00:09:25,985 --> 00:09:26,785
How did you find out?

210
00:09:26,810 --> 00:09:34,659
Oh, Iskineport posted it—Andres and
Anne, officially dating at Pers House!

211
00:09:34,684 --> 00:09:36,270
Secret only, huh?

212
00:09:36,295 --> 00:09:38,340
Like and subscribe!

213
00:09:38,940 --> 00:09:40,113
Yes, congrats!

214
00:09:40,138 --> 00:09:42,224
- Guys, guys, guys!
- Guys!

215
00:09:42,249 --> 00:09:43,463
Gu-guys!

216
00:09:43,488 --> 00:09:43,936
Oh?!

217
00:09:43,961 --> 00:09:45,416
Listen up!

218
00:09:45,441 --> 00:09:48,839
Okay! We’re listening! Speak up!

219
00:09:51,471 --> 00:09:53,271
Wait! Wait! Listen carefully!

220
00:09:53,296 --> 00:09:55,572
- You’re taking so long to say it!
- Anne!

221
00:09:55,597 --> 00:09:57,157
- Oh?
- And Andres!

222
00:09:57,287 --> 00:09:59,594
- What about them?
- They’re going on a date!

223
00:09:59,619 --> 00:10:01,344
- Yey!
- They’re going on a date!

224
00:10:01,975 --> 00:10:03,035
Do you understand?!

225
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,408
Ouch! Ouch!

226
00:10:04,663 --> 00:10:08,029
Good thing you got Kuya Iskineport
to delete that post right away.

227
00:10:09,503 --> 00:10:11,930
Has Tito Aga or Tita Cha seen it yet?

228
00:10:12,704 --> 00:10:16,158
No, because whenever I
talk to them, they seem fine.

229
00:10:16,417 --> 00:10:22,773
But the issue now is that Andres needs
some alone time to go on a date with Anne.

230
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,613
You know, for An-An.

231
00:10:24,638 --> 00:10:26,124
- Mmmm.
- Right?

232
00:10:26,985 --> 00:10:28,912
So, how can we help, Tash?

233
00:10:28,937 --> 00:10:33,603
Okay, we need to organize a date
at home—like a one-on-one dinner.

234
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:36,751
Kind of like a candlelit,
romantic setup, you know?

235
00:10:36,855 --> 00:10:37,595
- Oh!
- Mmm.

236
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:39,113
Actually, that would be romantic, right?

237
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:40,650
- Right?
- Yes.

238
00:10:41,992 --> 00:10:43,565
- Something romantic, like—
- You?

239
00:10:43,662 --> 00:10:46,275
My contribution will be
their outfits, of course!

240
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:51,477
I have a friend who thrifts
clothes, and I’ll glam them up!

241
00:10:51,844 --> 00:10:52,831
That works!

242
00:10:52,856 --> 00:10:55,299
Oh, and I’ll take care of the ambiance!

243
00:10:55,324 --> 00:10:59,995
I’ll handle the setup, the candles,
the flowers—I’m good at that!

244
00:11:00,082 --> 00:11:00,735
Perfect!

245
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:03,521
- It really is!
- Absolutely perfect!

246
00:11:03,590 --> 00:11:05,656
If you’re doing the ambiance,
I’ll take care of the music!

247
00:11:05,980 --> 00:11:07,600
Perfect timing—I know a DJ!

248
00:11:07,704 --> 00:11:09,397
- Oh!
- Then we’re all set!

249
00:11:09,422 --> 00:11:10,821
We really need to set the mood, right?

250
00:11:10,892 --> 00:11:14,338
- It’s their first date!
- I’ll take care of the food!

251
00:11:14,369 --> 00:11:15,009
Yes.

252
00:11:15,059 --> 00:11:17,740
Perfect! Oh my god,
they’re gonna be so happy!

253
00:11:17,765 --> 00:11:18,795
I’m excited!

254
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:20,284
And hopefully, we’ll be
happy with the payment

255
00:11:20,308 --> 00:11:21,772
too! Wait, how much
is our talent fee for this?

256
00:11:22,271 --> 00:11:23,291
Oh yeah, good point.

257
00:11:23,316 --> 00:11:24,229
Talent fee?

258
00:11:24,254 --> 00:11:25,140
- Yeah!
- Of course!

259
