Oh, this is a new technique.

514
00:23:20,003 --> 00:23:23,847
This feels just like how
my wife massages me!

515
00:23:23,872 --> 00:23:27,264
And sometimes I even get mad at her for it.

516
00:23:27,289 --> 00:23:29,494
But since it’s you,
it’s fine, keep going!

517
00:23:31,276 --> 00:23:32,736
Whoo, Charity!

518
00:23:33,069 --> 00:23:34,086
Where’s the music?

519
00:23:34,775 --> 00:23:35,868
There’s no music!

520
00:23:43,272 --> 00:23:46,660
Lower, lower, lower, lower!
Lower, lower, lower, lower!

521
00:23:50,168 --> 00:23:51,268
Are you okay?

522
00:23:53,889 --> 00:23:56,583
Tash, why are our more guests coming?

523
00:23:56,608 --> 00:23:57,286
It’s all on you now.

524
00:23:57,311 --> 00:23:58,411
How would I know?

525
00:23:59,101 --> 00:24:01,441
- I can’t control it anymore!
- Okay!

526
00:24:04,362 --> 00:24:06,009
What’s that? What’s that?

527
00:24:06,208 --> 00:24:07,701
Hi, everyone!

528
00:24:07,726 --> 00:24:10,590
- Hi!
- Hey!

529
00:24:12,811 --> 00:24:13,984
Oh, the rice!

530
00:24:14,208 --> 00:24:16,967
I heard there’s a party here!

531
00:24:16,992 --> 00:24:18,205
Osang told me.

532
00:24:18,849 --> 00:24:20,869
- Osang?!
- Osang!

533
00:24:20,894 --> 00:24:24,074
Why? Didn’t you say the more, the merrier?

534
00:24:24,154 --> 00:24:25,947
Hey!

535
00:24:27,057 --> 00:24:29,284
- I got the rice! Unlimited rice!
- Boss Beauty, thank you!

536
00:24:49,518 --> 00:24:50,406
Charity.

537
00:24:50,431 --> 00:24:52,084
- Yes?
- Where are you from?

538
00:24:52,397 --> 00:24:53,783
From Caloocan.

539
00:24:53,808 --> 00:24:54,828
Ah, Caloocan?

540
00:24:55,221 --> 00:24:55,787
Yes.

541
00:24:55,812 --> 00:24:58,965
I know a lot of people from there. A lot.

542
00:24:58,990 --> 00:25:00,344
- Oh, really?
- Yeah!

543
00:25:00,369 --> 00:25:04,199
You know, if I pass by
sometime… can I get your number?

544
00:25:04,849 --> 00:25:05,995
I’ll just get it later.

545
00:25:06,020 --> 00:25:08,197
- Uh…
- Is that okay?

546
00:25:08,248 --> 00:25:09,308
Sure.

547
00:25:09,333 --> 00:25:11,036
No, just so… you know.

548
00:25:11,061 --> 00:25:17,971
If I text you sometimes, if… you know, if
you ever have a problem, maybe I can help.

549
00:25:18,424 --> 00:25:20,908
Uh, you can also give
me your account number

550
00:25:20,932 --> 00:25:23,416
if that’s okay—ouch!
Your account number.

551
00:25:23,441 --> 00:25:27,968
What account number are you talking about?!

552
00:25:28,152 --> 00:25:30,239
Even my wife’s voice, you’re
starting to sound like her!

553
00:25:32,074 --> 00:25:34,387
Unbelievable. So, where’s
that account number?

554
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:35,190
What?!

555
00:25:35,215 --> 00:25:37,521
And you really asked again,
huh?! Account number?!

556
00:25:37,714 --> 00:25:39,403
What are you talking about?!

557
00:25:39,747 --> 00:25:41,052
Sounds just like my wife!

558
00:25:41,375 --> 00:25:43,622
What do you mean "sounds like"? Face me!

559
00:25:44,199 --> 00:25:45,247
My love!

560
00:25:45,648 --> 00:25:48,214
Wait, what?! What are you doing here?!

561
00:25:48,239 --> 00:25:50,149
What are you doing here?!
W-why is this happening?!

562
00:25:50,174 --> 00:25:52,433
You! What are you doing here?!

563
00:25:52,958 --> 00:25:54,716
Charity! Charity, she just—huh?!

564
00:25:55,087 --> 00:25:56,494
Uh…she came in.

565
00:25:56,519 --> 00:25:59,302
What’s this about asking for
account numbers, my love?!

566
00:25:59,327 --> 00:25:59,819
Account num—

567
00:25:59,844 --> 00:26:01,584
- And phone numbers?!
- My love, you don’t—

568
00:26:02,159 --> 00:26:02,972
- Hey!
- Hey!

569
00:26:02,997 --> 00:26:04,462
- BFF!
- That’s what I like!

570
00:26:04,487 --> 00:26:05,762
Good thing you showed up!

571
00:26:05,787 --> 00:26:06,906
- Oh, really?
- Yeah!

572
00:26:06,931 --> 00:26:08,286
What are you doing here?!

573
00:26:08,319 --> 00:26:09,672
I was just going to ask if
you were already fighting.

574
00:26:09,697 --> 00:26:10,998
So, are you breaking up?

575
00:26:11,023 --> 00:26:12,589
- No!
- No, we’re not. But…

576
00:26:12,614 --> 00:26:13,649
- Why would we break up?
- Yeah!

577
00:26:13,674 --> 00:26:15,879
What do you mean "but"? Look at you two—

578
00:26:15,904 --> 00:26:17,466
Not happening!

579
00:26:17,491 --> 00:26:19,538
You guys are such a mess!
You’re impossible to break up!

580
00:26:19,985 --> 00:26:22,958
Don’t! Don’t break us up! Even—

581
00:26:23,022 --> 00:26:27,459
Wait, before anything else, the reason I’m
here is because I was looking for you two.

582
00:26:27,484 --> 00:26:28,117
Why?

583
00:26:28,142 --> 00:26:29,594
Because I need to ask you for a favor, BFF.

584
00:26:29,619 --> 00:26:30,522
What?

585
00:26:30,547 --> 00:26:32,267
Can you talk to your son, Andres?

586
00:26:32,292 --> 00:26:36,104
Tell him to lower the
music at your house party.

587
00:26:36,197 --> 00:26:37,344
House party?!

588
00:26:37,369 --> 00:26:38,667
- There’s a house party?
- There’s a house party?

589
00:26:38,717 --> 00:26:40,075
- At your house.
- Huh?

590
00:26:40,133 --> 00:26:41,226
Don’t tell me you didn’t know?

591
00:26:41,268 --> 00:26:43,268
My love, what’s this? House party?

592
00:26:43,293 --> 00:26:45,392
- Did you know about this?
- No.

593
00:26:45,710 --> 00:26:47,196
You’re touching her?

594
00:26:47,221 --> 00:26:48,747
Why would she know? And
why are you holding onto her?!

595
00:26:48,772 --> 00:26:50,124
You’re even holding onto him!

596
00:26:59,132 --> 00:27:03,405
Thanks, Andres, ha? Our first date was fun.

597
00:27:04,193 --> 00:27:09,998
Anne, let’s make the most of the
time we have left before I leave.

598
00:27:43,609 --> 00:27:49,340
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey,
hey! What’s happening here, huh?!

599
00:27:50,328 --> 00:27:51,275
Everyone, go home!

600
00:27:51,734 --> 00:27:52,988
Anne, you too?!

601
00:27:53,581 --> 00:27:56,013
Stop the party! Go home!

602
00:27:56,952 --> 00:27:57,861
BFF.

603
00:27:57,886 --> 00:27:59,393
- Mm?
- This is my house.

604
00:27:59,939 --> 00:28:01,484
- Right.
- Can I be the one to say that?

605
00:28:01,922 --> 00:28:04,329
I was just practicing what you were
going to say. Go ahead, repeat it.

606
00:28:04,879 --> 00:28:06,213
Stop the party!

607
00:28:07,526 --> 00:28:08,569
Go home!

608
00:28:08,791 --> 00:28:11,425
Everyone, go home! Go, go, go!

609
00:28:12,671 --> 00:28:13,855
- Alright.
- Go home!

610
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:17,745
I was just about to hug my dance
partner… I haven’t even kissed her yet.

611
00:28:19,638 --> 00:28:20,938
Come on, Kuya Aga.

612
00:28:23,381 --> 00:28:25,853
- Ah, go home… let’s go home.
- Let’s go home. Dad, thanks, okay?

613
00:28:25,878 --> 00:28:27,173
Where do you think you’re going?

614
00:28:27,198 --> 00:28:28,160
They said they’re going home.

615
00:28:28,185 --> 00:28:29,326
No, stay here.

616
00:28:29,721 --> 00:28:32,614
Excuse me! BFF, even me?

617
00:28:33,645 --> 00:28:34,734
You too.

618
00:28:35,446 --> 00:28:36,334
Stop!

619
00:28:36,359 --> 00:28:37,413
- Stop.
- Me.

620
00:28:37,438 --> 00:28:39,099
- Me. Go.
- Bye!

621
00:28:40,261 --> 00:28:41,265
Thank you.

622
00:28:46,338 --> 00:28:47,468
Lola Maxi?

623
00:28:48,854 --> 00:28:50,147
Lola Maxi!

624
00:28:51,282 --> 00:28:52,254
What happened?

625
00:28:52,279 --> 00:28:53,473
Hey!

626
00:28:53,498 --> 00:28:54,741
- Hey!
- Hey!

627
00:28:54,766 --> 00:28:56,274
- Hey!
- What is this?!

628
00:28:57,047 --> 00:28:58,434
What’s happening?!

629
00:28:59,009 --> 00:28:59,920
Why?

630
00:28:59,945 --> 00:29:02,319
We’re having a party.
What’s wrong with that?

631
00:29:02,613 --> 00:29:04,726
My grandkids wanted to have fun.

632
00:29:04,751 --> 00:29:06,097
A party’s fun!

633
00:29:07,844 --> 00:29:08,944
What’s the problem?

634
00:29:17,547 --> 00:29:20,294
Well, then, let’s just party!

635
00:29:20,319 --> 00:29:21,986
- Alright.
- There’s nothing wrong with it, anyway…

636
00:29:22,011 --> 00:29:23,308
- Let’s keep going!
- Oh!

637
00:29:23,333 --> 00:29:24,194
Let’s have fun!

638
00:29:24,219 --> 00:29:25,278
That’s right!

639
00:29:25,303 --> 00:29:27,905
- Lower!
- Lower! Turn it up!

640
00:29:28,184 --> 00:29:29,264
Lower!

641
00:29:29,289 --> 00:29:31,287
- Lower! Lower!
- Lower!

642
00:29:34,431 --> 00:29:35,438
Sorry, Dad.

643
00:29:36,499 --> 00:29:40,591
I was just waiting for the right time to
tell you and Mom about me and Anne.

644
00:29:41,945 --> 00:29:42,848
The timing was never right.

645
00:29:47,864 --> 00:29:51,551
Lola Maxi, did you know about this?

646
00:29:53,267 --> 00:30:01,848
Aga, Cha, these kids are grown-ups
now. My grandson is at the right age.

647
00:30:02,249 --> 00:30:05,375
And Anne is a good girl, right?

648
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:08,792
You know her. She’s beautiful.

649
00:30:08,817 --> 00:30:09,279
Mmm.

650
00:30:09,304 --> 00:30:13,338
Kind, hardworking, respectful.

651
00:30:13,828 --> 00:30:16,155
My grandson has good taste.

652
00:30:16,285 --> 00:30:18,785
I don’t have a problem with it.

653
00:30:19,638 --> 00:30:20,771
It’s fine with me.

654
00:30:21,504 --> 00:30:24,165
Actually, I’ve thought
about it—I know that

655
00:30:24,189 --> 00:30:27,422
Atasha and Andres are
already of the right age.

656
00:30:28,007 --> 00:30:30,867
So…what else can I do, right?

657
00:30:31,027 --> 00:30:34,733
All I ask is that next
time, just let us know.

658
00:30:36,596 --> 00:30:39,876
Because yeah—it’s really okay. Right?

659
00:30:40,456 --> 00:30:41,462
Sorry.

660
00:30:46,192 --> 00:30:48,972
Um, one more thing, Dad—

661
00:30:49,443 --> 00:30:50,266
Mmm?

662
00:30:55,766 --> 00:30:58,413
We got a job offer from Singapore.

663
00:30:59,435 --> 00:31:00,868
We have to go back.

664
00:31:02,292 --> 00:31:02,925
Ooh.

665
00:31:03,324 --> 00:31:08,404
Ooh. You know, Atasha, Andres,

666
00:31:09,927 --> 00:31:13,079
you’ve already helped
me and your Dad so much,

667
00:31:14,608 --> 00:31:21,732
so whatever you decide, we’ll accept it.

668
00:31:23,566 --> 00:31:24,574
Thanks, Mom.

669
00:31:24,599 --> 00:31:25,945
- Thank you.
- Thank you, love you.

670
00:31:35,020 --> 00:31:37,460
Uh, what about us?

671
00:31:38,286 --> 00:31:39,299
It’s like we don’t matter, huh?

672
00:31:41,060 --> 00:31:45,349
Ah, right. Um, Lola
Maxi, thank you so much.

673
00:31:45,374 --> 00:31:46,626
- Mmm.
- Thank you so much.

674
00:31:50,763 --> 00:31:52,014
What?

675
00:31:52,039 --> 00:31:54,160
Of course, we saved the best for last—

676
00:31:54,604 --> 00:31:55,440
thank you, Dad!

677
00:31:55,465 --> 00:31:56,456
Thank you, Dad!

678
00:31:57,231 --> 00:31:58,731
You’re enjoying this aren’t you?

679
00:32:00,733 --> 00:32:03,159
Dad, you’re blushing a little.

680
00:32:04,531 --> 00:32:06,258
You all saw it, right?

681
00:32:07,019 --> 00:32:14,204
Through problems and joy…
Pers is always first, Pers is the star!

682
00:32:18,347 --> 00:32:21,134
Tso K, are you mad at me?

683
00:32:23,208 --> 00:32:24,175
I’m not mad!

684
00:32:25,389 --> 00:32:28,509
But of course, it’s a little sad.

685
00:32:29,475 --> 00:32:33,161
Another woman is leaving
my life because of Aga.

686
00:32:36,443 --> 00:32:39,816
Tso K, come on, I’m not leaving.

687
00:32:40,528 --> 00:32:42,448
We’re just adding
more to the family.

688
00:32:44,196 --> 00:32:45,319
Adding?

689
00:32:45,673 --> 00:32:46,811
You’re pregnant?!

690
00:32:46,964 --> 00:32:48,107
You better behave!

691
00:32:48,132 --> 00:32:51,532
No, Tso K! That was a joke!

692
00:32:52,133 --> 00:32:53,295
Watch it, you!

693
00:32:53,877 --> 00:32:55,151
It was just a joke!

694
00:32:55,347 --> 00:32:58,821
Well…actually, I do know Andres.

695
00:32:59,093 --> 00:33:02,266
Honestly, I know he’s a good guy.

696
00:33:03,072 --> 00:33:05,825
He’s polite and kind.

697
00:33:06,587 --> 00:33:08,000
Alright, fine, I’m okay with it.

698
00:33:08,773 --> 00:33:09,954
You’re okay now, Tso K?

699
00:33:09,979 --> 00:33:10,832
- Mmm.
- We’re good?

700
00:33:10,863 --> 00:33:12,136
- Yeah.
- Andres!

701
00:33:12,309 --> 00:33:14,096
- It’s all good! Come here!
- That was fast.

702
00:33:14,394 --> 00:33:15,288
He was just right there?

703
00:33:15,813 --> 00:33:16,800
Ah…

704
00:33:18,479 --> 00:33:18,972
Whoa!

705
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:23,046
Tso K, I’m here to formally court Anne.

706
00:33:23,839 --> 00:33:25,194
We’re going to serenade her!

707
00:33:25,337 --> 00:33:26,475
Right, guys?!

708
00:33:28,529 --> 00:33:29,669
Let’s go, An-An!

709
00:33:35,664 --> 00:33:37,484
Maestro, give me some music!

710
00:33:38,046 --> 00:33:39,473
Just let him do it!

711
00:33:39,498 --> 00:33:42,467
You good? Just let him go for it.

712
00:33:43,081 --> 00:33:44,169
Okay?

713
00:33:44,194 --> 00:33:45,388
Alright, alright, alright!

714
00:33:46,142 --> 00:33:50,195
But if you’re off-key, I’ll gong you!

715
00:33:51,702 --> 00:33:52,755
Let’s hear it!

716
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:54,055
You gotta help me here, okay?!

717
00:33:58,049 --> 00:34:01,782
<i>♪ No need to force… ♪</i>

718
00:34:01,807 --> 00:34:02,961
Wow!

719
00:34:02,986 --> 00:34:07,928
<i>♪ …someone like me, oh, I’m all yours. ♪</i>

720
00:34:07,953 --> 00:34:09,021
Come on, you got this!

721
00:34:09,053 --> 00:34:20,607
<i>♪ …even if you’re not really mine, oh, I’m
all yours, just take care of my heart. ♪</i>

722
00:34:20,798 --> 00:34:28,183
<i>♪ I’m not forcing myself on you… ♪</i>

723
00:34:28,631 --> 00:34:29,698
Such a dad moment, huh?

724
00:34:29,723 --> 00:34:33,661
<i>♪ Can you hear it?
Do me a favor, please? ♪</i>

725
00:34:35,805 --> 00:34:36,964
Okay, Tash—

726
00:34:37,562 --> 00:34:39,629
You’re so good! Go, An-An!

727
00:34:41,450 --> 00:34:42,350
Anne…

728
00:34:42,375 --> 00:34:45,301
<i>♪ Do me a favor… ♪</i>

729
00:34:49,867 --> 00:34:54,616
Your friends look so shy…they
all look so embarrassed!

730
00:34:54,641 --> 00:34:56,763
Do me a favor, oh…

731
00:35:01,121 --> 00:35:06,858
♪ Do me a favor, do me a favor… ♪

732
00:35:06,883 --> 00:35:08,020
Okay!

733
00:35:12,214 --> 00:35:13,727
Amazing!

734
00:35:13,752 --> 00:35:15,311
Well?! Well, Karl? Does he pass?

735
00:35:15,775 --> 00:35:17,388
With flying colors!

736
00:35:18,888 --> 00:35:22,693
I have a partner, she’s
great at tattooing—Jen!

737
00:35:22,817 --> 00:35:24,311
Who wants a tattoo?!

738
00:35:24,456 --> 00:35:26,020
- Me!
- Us!

739
00:35:26,045 --> 00:35:28,219
Sure! You go first!

740
00:35:28,244 --> 00:35:29,805
Are you really using that?!

741
00:35:29,830 --> 00:35:31,074
Yes!

742
00:35:31,417 --> 00:35:34,973
Did you notice the kids’
passports? They’re missing.

743
00:35:35,010 --> 00:35:36,555
You’re not leaving anymore?

744
00:35:37,318 --> 00:35:38,505
No, Lola.

745
00:35:38,530 --> 00:35:39,806
I already found my love.

746
00:35:39,831 --> 00:35:42,405
I already have my
Che-che. In fairness, huh?

747
00:35:42,430 --> 00:35:43,162
What?

748
00:35:43,187 --> 00:35:44,546
She looks like you.

749
00:35:44,571 --> 00:35:45,564
Is that real?

750
00:35:45,589 --> 00:35:51,003
There’s no Che-che that
exists in Barangay Singko.

751
00:35:51,028 --> 00:35:53,294
- Che-che is real!
- Right?!

752
00:35:53,319 --> 00:35:54,618
But…she was paid for.

753
00:35:54,643 --> 00:35:57,541
I’ll prove it to you! Watch!
Give me a tattoo.

754
00:35:57,971 --> 00:35:59,491
Write "Che-che"!

755
00:36:00,530 --> 00:36:01,523
Oh!
